    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0259" n="235" xml:id="pg235"/>

                <head>Mr. Sanford to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 177.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 14, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to enclose herewith some
                    data I have collected with regard to the recruiting system in this country, and
                    with especial reference to cases of exemptions, as likely to be of use at this
                    moment when our law on the subject is being revised.</p>
                <p>I have thought that, in this connexion, some details touching the systems of
                    France and Prussia, and their workings, would not be without interest and
                    perhaps value, and have accordingly included them in the accompanying paper.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. S. SANFORD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State,</hi> &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d208-a1.xml" xpointer="d208-a1"/>
            </div>
